# until a shell or systemd reads it: a variable or a command's output ($f, ${IFS}, $(...), `...`), a glob (* ? [), a
# brace, a backslash (an escape: systemd reads \x77 and \s in a unit), a control character, U+FFFD (bytes that are no
# UTF-8), any other sign. So does a tilde at a word's start or after = or : (HOME_TILDE: ~backup/pw, ~/pw: a service
# user's home may be outside /home, where jobs see it). Such a word fails closed (Unsure). But a LOCKED file in the
